            <ArticleTitle>Does elevated cardiac troponin I in patients with unstable angina predict ischemia on stress testing?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1440-2, A6, A8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To help guide physicians in their evaluation of patients with acute coronary syndromes, we investigated whether elevated cardiac troponin I in patients presenting with unstable angina predicts ischemia on stress testing. Elevated cardiac troponin I in patients who present with chest pain and normal creatine kinase levels is associated with ischemia on stress testing, as well as with future cardiac events.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
